+# CYB0X-S — seven-palette theme recovery
+
+This folder is a **self-contained, portable copy** of the theme work so it can be
+rebuilt in any fresh checkout. Both artifacts are generated from the commit
+`fb512de` (parent `aafa2c5`), which is the current tip of
+`arena/01a05f18-cyb0x-s`.
+
+## Contents
+
+| File | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `0001-theme-seven-palettes.patch` | The `fb512de` commit as a unified diff (README + `src/cyb0x_s/tui/theme.py`). |
+| `theme-recovery.bundle` | The same commit in a git bundle, preserving the **original commit hash** `fb512de`. |
+| `REBUILD.md` | This file. |
+
+## Verified
+
+* `git bundle verify theme-recovery.bundle` → **okay**: contains `fb512de`
+  (refs/heads/arena/01a05f18-cyb0x-s), requires `aafa2c5`.
+* `git apply --check 0001-theme-seven-palettes.patch` on a fresh checkout of
+  `aafa2c5` → **applies cleanly**.
+* With the patch applied, `src/cyb0x_s/tui/theme.py` defines **7 palettes**
+  (`name=` × 7).
+* Applied on a checkout of the *base* `aafa2c5` — do **not** apply it on
+  `e7e3047` (or any state that already contains the two-palette `Palette`
+  design plus a picker), where hunks may conflict.
+
+## Recovery commands
+
+### Option A — apply the patch onto the base commit
+
+```bash
+git checkout -B arena/01a05f18-cyb0x-s aafa2c5
+git apply handoff/0001-theme-seven-palettes.patch
+git commit -am "feat(theme): restore all seven palettes with WCAG AAA/AA contrast"
+```
+
+### Option B — restore exact hashes from the bundle
+
+```bash
+git fetch handoff/theme-recovery.bundle
+git checkout -b arena/01a05f18-cyb0x-s FETCH_HEAD
+# or, to keep it as a commit on top of current state:
+git cherry-pick fb512deb558fc1f53314112bd08f8314ff38cba1
+```
+
+## What this contains
+
+* **Seven palettes**: `slate` (default), `midnight`, `ember`, `moss`, `neon`,
+  `mono`, `warm`.
+* **`Palette` methods**: `_luminance()`, `contrast_ratio()`, `swatch()`.
+* **Module helpers**: `mix()`, `ramp()` (used by the gradient bar).
+* **README** updated to list the seven themes with their commands and the
+  AAA/AA contrast guarantee.
+
+Verified contrast (text on bg — all AAA ≥7:1; muted AA ≥4.5:1):
+
+| theme | text | muted | accent |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| slate | 14.69 | 6.25 | 10.70 |
+| midnight | 14.74 | 5.53 | 7.84 |
+| ember | 15.75 | 6.31 | 10.49 |
+| moss | 15.14 | 6.14 | 10.43 |
+| neon | 16.68 | 5.70 | 7.46 |
+| mono | 17.85 | 6.02 | 16.29 |
+| warm | 13.37 | 6.44 | 5.31 |
+
+## Not included (available on request)
+
+The theme **picker modal** (`ThemeSwatch` / `ThemePickerModal`, `T` →
+`action_open_theme_picker`), the `settings.py` derive-guidance gate, and the
+`dev/theme_gallery.py` gallery tool were described in the previous handoff but
+their exact source is not present, so they were not reconstructed here. The
+palettes are fully selectable already via `:theme <name>` and the `T` cycle.
